  "answer": "## What’s happening (mechanism)

`MenuItem` is built on top of `ListItem`. The focus-visible styling is handled inside `ListItem` only when `button={true}`.

In `ListItem`, the `focusVisibleClassName` prop is wired directly into the underlying `ButtonBase`:

- In `packages/material-ui/src/ListItem/ListItem.js`, when `button` is true it does:
  - `componentProps.focusVisibleClassName = classes.focusVisible`
  - and renders `Component = ButtonBase` (so `focusVisibleClassName` becomes a `ButtonBase` prop). (see `packages/material-ui/src/ListItem/ListItem.js`, lines ~70–105 in the provided excerpt)

```js
if (button) {
  componentProps.component = componentProp || 'div';
  componentProps.focusVisibleClassName = classes.focusVisible;
  Component = ButtonBase;
}
```

So the “class name that gets applied” is not taken from the incoming props; it’s always forced to `classes.focusVisible` from `ListItem`’s own styling.

## Why `MenuItem`’s `focusVisibleClassName` prop appears ignored

`ListItem` does **not** forward/consume a `focusVisibleClassName` provided by the caller. Instead, it overwrites it whenever `button` is enabled.

Therefore, if `MenuItem` accepts a `focusVisibleClassName` prop (for typing), but `MenuItem` ultimately renders a `ListItem` with `button`, `ListItem` will overwrite the prop value with its internal `classes.focusVisible` (from `packages/material-ui/src/ListItem/ListItem.js`, `focusVisible: { ... }` in the `styles()` block).

## Files involved

- `packages/material-ui/src/ListItem/ListItem.js`
  - defines `classes.focusVisible` in `styles()` (focus-visible background)
  - overwrites `componentProps.focusVisibleClassName` when `button` is true
- `packages/material-ui/src/MenuItem/MenuItem.js`
  - likely forwards props to `ListItem`, but the critical behavior is in `ListItem` overwriting the class name.

## Practical takeaway

To make `MenuItem` respect `focusVisibleClassName`, `ListItem` would need to *use the incoming prop* when provided (instead of always setting `classes.focusVisible`).",
